# Kafka tests

Put tests in the module you change. Prefer a unit test. Use a cluster test only when the behavior needs a running broker.

## JUnit 5

Use JUnit Jupiter (`org.junit.jupiter.api`). Do not add JUnit 4 tests.

Assertions come from `org.junit.jupiter.api.Assertions` (`assertEquals`, `assertThrows`, and the other `assert*` methods). This repo does not use AssertJ.

Name the test after the behavior (`testCannotSendToInternalTopic`, `shouldRestoreNullRecord`).

Gradle splits suites by tag (`build.gradle`):

- `@Tag("integration")` runs in `integrationTest` and is excluded from `unitTest`.
- Methods without that tag run in `unitTest`.

```bash
./gradlew :clients:test --tests org.apache.kafka.clients.MetadataTest
./gradlew :clients:test --tests org.apache.kafka.clients.MetadataTest.testTimeToNextUpdate
```

`scripts/simulate_ci.sh --module <module> --tests <filter>` runs Checkstyle and that test filter together.

## Mockito

Mockito is on the test classpath. Create mocks with `Mockito.mock` / `mock`, stub with `when(...).thenReturn(...)`, and check interactions with `verify`. Do not add another mocking library.

Prefer deterministic fakes already in the tree (`MockTime`, test utilities under `org.apache.kafka.test` or the module's test helpers) over `Thread.sleep` or a live socket.

## Cluster tests

The framework is documented in `test-common/test-common-internal-api/src/main/java/org/apache/kafka/common/test/api/README.md`. `ClusterTestExtensions` is registered through SPI. Do not add `@ExtendWith` for it.

- `@ClusterTest` declares one cluster. `@ClusterTests` declares several. `@ClusterTemplate("methodName")` points at a static method returning `List<ClusterConfig>`.
- `@ClusterTestDefaults` sets class-level defaults.
- Inject `ClusterInstance` as a test-method parameter or as a constructor argument when `@BeforeEach` needs the cluster. The same instance is passed either way.
- The cluster starts before `@BeforeEach` when `autoStart` is left at its default.
- `ClusterConfig` is immutable inside the test method.

Do not combine `@ClusterTest` / `@ClusterTests` / `@ClusterTemplate` with `@ParameterizedTest`. A plain `@Test` method does not start a cluster and does not receive `ClusterInstance`.

```java
@ClusterTest(brokers = 3)
void testSomething(ClusterInstance cluster) {
    cluster.admin().createTopics(...);
}
```

## Flakes

A test that is intentionally skipped on normal runs carries `@Flaky` and a JIRA id, for example `@Flaky("KAFKA-13514")`. Those tests stay out of the default run unless `-Pkafka.test.run.flaky=true`. Do not delete an assertion or add a retry loop to hide a failure.

Test log verbosity is `log4j2.yaml` under that module's `src/test/resources/`.
